{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgdxWnWLXgayZjKysUtkLf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 187,\n3\t \"title\": \"[Bug]: webContents.debugger use-after-free: cppgc-managed Debugger never detaches its DevToolsAgentHostClient, crashing the browser process\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n41.5.0 (also reproduced on 43.4.1)\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nmacOS\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nmacOS 26.6.2\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\narm64 (including Apple Silicon)\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\nUnknown — the affected code path was introduced with the cppgc/Oilpan migration of `electron::api::Debugger`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAttaching `webContents.debugger` to a WebContents (in our case, `<webview>` guest contents), receiving CDP notifications, and later letting the WebContents be destroyed should never crash the browser process, regardless of GC timing.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nThe browser process segfaults (`EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS` at `0x10`/`0x18` — a null/dangling pointer plus member offset) on `CrBrowserMain`. We collected three crashes in one day across two Electron versions (41.5.0 and 43.4.1), in two distinct but related signatures.\\n\\n**Signature A (2 of 3 crashes) — inbound CDP notification dispatched to a freed client** (symbolicated from macOS `.ips` via breakpad symbols, Electron 41.5.0):\\n\\n```\\n0  content::DevToolsSession::DispatchProtocolNotification(...)\\n1  blink::mojom::DevToolsSessionHostStubDispatch::Accept(...)\\n2  mojo::InterfaceEndpointClient::HandleIncomingMessageThunk::Accept(mojo::Message*)\\n3  mojo::MessageDispatcher::Accept(mojo::Message*)\\n4  mojo::InterfaceEndpointClient::HandleIncomingMessage(mojo::Message*)\\n5  IPC::ChannelAssociatedGroupController::AcceptOnEndpointThread(...)\\n6  base::TaskAnnotator::RunTaskImpl(base::PendingTask&)\\n7  base::sequence_manager::internal::ThreadControllerWithMessagePumpImpl::DoWork()\\n8  base::MessagePumpCFRunLoopBase::RunWorkSource(void*)\\n   ... CFRunLoop / NSApplication run loop ...\\n```\\n\\nOn 43.4.1 the same crash appears with frame 0 in `content::DevToolsSession::DispatchProtocolResponseOrNotification(content::DevToolsAgentHostClient*, ...)`.\\n\\n**Signature B (1 of 3) — WebContents teardown force-detaches sessions into a freed client** (Electron 41.5.0):\\n\\n```\\n0  content::DevToolsAgentHostImpl::ForceDetachAllSessionsImpl()\\n1  content::RenderFrameDevToolsAgentHost::DestroyOnRenderFrameGone()\\n2  content::RenderFrameDevToolsAgentHost::FrameDeleted(...)\\n3  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsObserverList::NotifyObservers(...)\\n4  content::WebContentsImpl::OnFrameTreeNodeDestroyed(content::FrameTreeNode*)\\n5  content::FrameTree::Shutdown()\\n6  content::WebContentsImpl::~WebContentsImpl()\\n7  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::DestroyOwnedInnerWebContents(...)\\n8  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::DetachInnerWebContents(...)\\n9  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::OnFrameTreeNodeDestroyed(...)\\n10 content::FrameTreeNode::~FrameTreeNode()\\n11 content::RenderFrameHostImpl::ResetChildren()\\n12 content::FrameTree::Shutdown()\\n13 content::WebContentsImpl::~WebContentsImpl()\\n14 electron::InspectableWebContents::~InspectableWebContents()\\n15 electron::api::WebContents::~WebContents()\\n16 electron::api::WebContents::DeleteThisIfAlive()\\n17 base::TaskAnnotator::RunTaskImpl(base::PendingTask&)\\n   ... message pump ...\\n```\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n**Root-cause analysis** (from reading the v41.5.0 / main sources; we do not have a minimal repro yet — the crash depends on GC timing, which matches its \\\"random, tens of minutes apart\\\" occurrence in production):\\n\\n`electron::api::Debugger` is now a cppgc/Oilpan-managed `gin::Wrappable`, but it registers itself with content as a **raw** `content::DevToolsAgentHostClient*` via `agent_host_->AttachClient(this)`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L119\\n\\nIts destructor never detaches that client:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L35\\n\\n```cc\\nDebugger::~Debugger() = default;\\n```\\n\\n`DetachClient` is only called from the explicit JS-facing `Debugger::Detach()`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L126-L131\\n\\nThe only strong root keeping an attached `Debugger` alive is the owning `api::WebContents`'s member:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h#L783\\n\\n```cc\\ncppgc::Persistent<api::Debugger> debugger_;\\n```\\n\\nSo once the `api::WebContents` wrapper goes away (e.g. `<webview>` guest destruction via the posted `DeleteThisIfAlive()` task, as in Signature B), nothing on the content side owns or pins the still-attached client. When cppgc sweeps the `Debugger` while `DevToolsSession`/`DevToolsAgentHost` still hold the raw client pointer:\\n\\n- the next CDP notification from the renderer dispatches into freed memory (**Signature A** — easy to hit with chatty domains like `Network.enable` / `Log.enable` / `Page.startScreencast`), or\\n- a later WebContents-tree teardown reaches `ForceDetachAllSessionsImpl()`, which invokes `client->AgentHostClosed()` on freed memory (**Signature B**). Sweep order between the `api::WebContents` and its `Debugger` in the same GC cycle is unspecified, so the Debugger can be gone by the time the WebContents teardown runs.\\n\\nThe bug is still present on `main` — `Debugger::~Debugger() = default;`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L36\\n\\nBefore the cppgc migration this was masked because the wrappable's deterministic destruction paths differed; with Oilpan, destruction is decoupled from the last use, so the raw client pointer in content outlives the object.\\n\\n**Suggested fix**: ensure the client is detached before the object can be reclaimed — e.g. call `agent_host_->DetachClient(this)` in `~Debugger()` (mirroring `Detach()`), and/or detach in a `WebContentsDestroyed()` observer hook so the session never survives its client.\\n\\n**Context in which we hit this**: our app attaches `webContents.debugger.attach(\\\"1.3\\\")` to `<webview>` guest WebContents and enables `Runtime`/`Network`/`Log`/`Accessibility` (constant notification stream). Guests are routinely destroyed and recreated. Crashes appear minutes to tens of minutes later, aligned with GC pressure rather than any user action. Happy to provide the full `.ips` reports or symbolicated dumps on request.\\n\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"43-x-y\",\n7\t  \"needs-template\",\n8\t  \"platform/macOS\"\n9\t ],\n10\t \"state\": \"open\",\n11\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n12\t \"as_of\": \"2026-09-01T17:16:21Z\",\n13\t \"replay\": true\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd2d9b2-968e-4c5d-be3c-d122ad20270c","uuid":"7f175255-b18b-49e9-bc40-a1b47ad13e7d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T12:40:12.995Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 187,\n \"title\": \"[Bug]: webContents.debugger use-after-free: cppgc-managed Debugger never detaches its DevToolsAgentHostClient, crashing the browser process\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n41.5.0 (also reproduced on 43.4.1)\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nmacOS\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nmacOS 26.6.2\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\narm64 (including Apple Silicon)\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\nUnknown — the affected code path was introduced with the cppgc/Oilpan migration of `electron::api::Debugger`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAttaching `webContents.debugger` to a WebContents (in our case, `<webview>` guest contents), receiving CDP notifications, and later letting the WebContents be destroyed should never crash the browser process, regardless of GC timing.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nThe browser process segfaults (`EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS` at `0x10`/`0x18` — a null/dangling pointer plus member offset) on `CrBrowserMain`. We collected three crashes in one day across two Electron versions (41.5.0 and 43.4.1), in two distinct but related signatures.\\n\\n**Signature A (2 of 3 crashes) — inbound CDP notification dispatched to a freed client** (symbolicated from macOS `.ips` via breakpad symbols, Electron 41.5.0):\\n\\n```\\n0  content::DevToolsSession::DispatchProtocolNotification(...)\\n1  blink::mojom::DevToolsSessionHostStubDispatch::Accept(...)\\n2  mojo::InterfaceEndpointClient::HandleIncomingMessageThunk::Accept(mojo::Message*)\\n3  mojo::MessageDispatcher::Accept(mojo::Message*)\\n4  mojo::InterfaceEndpointClient::HandleIncomingMessage(mojo::Message*)\\n5  IPC::ChannelAssociatedGroupController::AcceptOnEndpointThread(...)\\n6  base::TaskAnnotator::RunTaskImpl(base::PendingTask&)\\n7  base::sequence_manager::internal::ThreadControllerWithMessagePumpImpl::DoWork()\\n8  base::MessagePumpCFRunLoopBase::RunWorkSource(void*)\\n   ... CFRunLoop / NSApplication run loop ...\\n```\\n\\nOn 43.4.1 the same crash appears with frame 0 in `content::DevToolsSession::DispatchProtocolResponseOrNotification(content::DevToolsAgentHostClient*, ...)`.\\n\\n**Signature B (1 of 3) — WebContents teardown force-detaches sessions into a freed client** (Electron 41.5.0):\\n\\n```\\n0  content::DevToolsAgentHostImpl::ForceDetachAllSessionsImpl()\\n1  content::RenderFrameDevToolsAgentHost::DestroyOnRenderFrameGone()\\n2  content::RenderFrameDevToolsAgentHost::FrameDeleted(...)\\n3  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsObserverList::NotifyObservers(...)\\n4  content::WebContentsImpl::OnFrameTreeNodeDestroyed(content::FrameTreeNode*)\\n5  content::FrameTree::Shutdown()\\n6  content::WebContentsImpl::~WebContentsImpl()\\n7  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::DestroyOwnedInnerWebContents(...)\\n8  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::DetachInnerWebContents(...)\\n9  content::WebContentsImpl::WebContentsTreeNode::OnFrameTreeNodeDestroyed(...)\\n10 content::FrameTreeNode::~FrameTreeNode()\\n11 content::RenderFrameHostImpl::ResetChildren()\\n12 content::FrameTree::Shutdown()\\n13 content::WebContentsImpl::~WebContentsImpl()\\n14 electron::InspectableWebContents::~InspectableWebContents()\\n15 electron::api::WebContents::~WebContents()\\n16 electron::api::WebContents::DeleteThisIfAlive()\\n17 base::TaskAnnotator::RunTaskImpl(base::PendingTask&)\\n   ... message pump ...\\n```\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n**Root-cause analysis** (from reading the v41.5.0 / main sources; we do not have a minimal repro yet — the crash depends on GC timing, which matches its \\\"random, tens of minutes apart\\\" occurrence in production):\\n\\n`electron::api::Debugger` is now a cppgc/Oilpan-managed `gin::Wrappable`, but it registers itself with content as a **raw** `content::DevToolsAgentHostClient*` via `agent_host_->AttachClient(this)`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L119\\n\\nIts destructor never detaches that client:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L35\\n\\n```cc\\nDebugger::~Debugger() = default;\\n```\\n\\n`DetachClient` is only called from the explicit JS-facing `Debugger::Detach()`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L126-L131\\n\\nThe only strong root keeping an attached `Debugger` alive is the owning `api::WebContents`'s member:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v41.5.0/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h#L783\\n\\n```cc\\ncppgc::Persistent<api::Debugger> debugger_;\\n```\\n\\nSo once the `api::WebContents` wrapper goes away (e.g. `<webview>` guest destruction via the posted `DeleteThisIfAlive()` task, as in Signature B), nothing on the content side owns or pins the still-attached client. When cppgc sweeps the `Debugger` while `DevToolsSession`/`DevToolsAgentHost` still hold the raw client pointer:\\n\\n- the next CDP notification from the renderer dispatches into freed memory (**Signature A** — easy to hit with chatty domains like `Network.enable` / `Log.enable` / `Page.startScreencast`), or\\n- a later WebContents-tree teardown reaches `ForceDetachAllSessionsImpl()`, which invokes `client->AgentHostClosed()` on freed memory (**Signature B**). Sweep order between the `api::WebContents` and its `Debugger` in the same GC cycle is unspecified, so the Debugger can be gone by the time the WebContents teardown runs.\\n\\nThe bug is still present on `main` — `Debugger::~Debugger() = default;`:\\nhttps://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/shell/browser/api/electron_api_debugger.cc#L36\\n\\nBefore the cppgc migration this was masked because the wrappable's deterministic destruction paths differed; with Oilpan, destruction is decoupled from the last use, so the raw client pointer in content outlives the object.\\n\\n**Suggested fix**: ensure the client is detached before the object can be reclaimed — e.g. call `agent_host_->DetachClient(this)` in `~Debugger()` (mirroring `Detach()`), and/or detach in a `WebContentsDestroyed()` observer hook so the session never survives its client.\\n\\n**Context in which we hit this**: our app attaches `webContents.debugger.attach(\\\"1.3\\\")` to `<webview>` guest WebContents and enables `Runtime`/`Network`/`Log`/`Accessibility` (constant notification stream). Guests are routinely destroyed and recreated. Crashes appear minutes to tens of minutes later, aligned with GC pressure rather than any user action. Happy to provide the full `.ips` reports or symbolicated dumps on request.\\n\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"43-x-y\",\n  \"needs-template\",\n  \"platform/macOS\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-09-01T17:16:21Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TgdxWnWLXgayZjKysUtkLf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
